# ============================================================================
#  What does NOT go into the image
# ============================================================================
#
# The two that matter are secrets and state:
#
#   `.env*`      — a laptop's `.env.local` holds the World ID client secret and
#                  the signing key. Copying it in would put both in a layer and
#                  make the image decide its own public URL.
#   `*.db*`      — the local demo database. In the image it would ship one
#                  deployment's queue state to the next one, and the volume is
#                  where the database belongs anyway.
#
# `certificates/` is a private key for the local HTTPS dev server, and
# `.test-db/` is the test suite's scratch space. Neither has any business in a
# container that a platform builds and stores.
.dockerignore

# Secrets and local configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
certificates/
*.pem

# Local state
db/*.db
db/*.db-wal
db/*.db-shm
.test-db/
var/

# Build output and caches — the image builds these itself, from source
.next
node_modules
.npm-cache
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Repository furniture
.git
.gitignore
.github
*.md
!README.md
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
